<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŏnĭtum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		moneo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>admonition, advice, counsel</i> (rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meis consiliis, monitis, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 5, 8, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tuis monitis praeceptisque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 13, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meas aures omnium praeceptis monitisque
					patuisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Phil. 14, 7, 20</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Job, 1, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Deut.
				21, 20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A prophecy, prediction</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deorum monita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Har. Resp. 25, 54</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carmentis Nymphae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 336</span></i>
			.</div>
